# REA on cloud and mobile

Reverse engineering with REA needs **both** the repo skill and the **rea** MCP server on **this run**.

## New chat / new agent run

Cloud and iOS agents **do not** copy MCP choices from earlier chats. Each new run starts with MCP servers **off** until you turn them on.

Before the first message on a new mobile or cloud run:

1. Open **+ → MCP Servers** and enable **rea** (same account as cursor.com/agents).
2. Use branch **main** so `.cursor/skills/reverse-engineer-anything/` is present.
3. For REA-heavy work, invoke **`/reverse-engineer-anything`** so the workflow loads explicitly.

## If REA tools are missing

When the tool list has no `rea` / REA MCP tools, **stop and tell the user**:

- They must **start a new agent run** (or go back to launch) and enable **rea** under **MCP Servers** before continuing.
- Skills alone do not add MCP tools; dashboard MCP registration does not auto-enable per run on mobile.

Do not pretend REA analysis is available without those tools.
